# No duplicate slice or worktree agents (HARD)

Launching a "fresh" or "redo" agent while another is still bound to the same ticket or worktree
races the tree, doubles the cost and throws away the first agent's work. This is not a soft
preference.

## Forbidden

```text
❌ A sub-agent for ticket <id> while any earlier sub-agent for <id> is still running
❌ A "fresh redo" / "interrupt and take over" / second agent on the same
   .ai/artifacts/worktrees/<id> because the first looks slow or stuck
❌ Parallel agents that both write the same file (tools_v2/xtask/src/main.rs, or any path in
   the ticket's owns list) for the same ticket, even if you think the first is idle
❌ Reading a short transcript, a long silence or "only untracked files" as permission to spawn
   a replacement
```

## Required instead

1. **One agent per ticket worktree until it completes or the operator says to kill it.**
2. If it looks stuck: **wait**, or ask the operator one line — do **not** spawn a twin.
3. To nudge a live agent: resume **that same agent id** only (no interrupt unless the operator
   explicitly says interrupt, kill or replace).
4. Before dispatching a new sub-agent for ticket `<id>`, check that no sub-agent for `<id>` is
   still in flight in this conversation. If one is → **do not dispatch**.
5. The factory's orchestrator gates, lands and verifies completed commits only; it never "helps" a
   live slice agent by opening a second coding agent on its tree
   ([Factory waves](/documentation_v2/runbooks/factory_waves/README.md)).

## Operator override (the only legal exception)

The operator must **explicitly** say to kill or replace that agent, for example "kill `<id>` and
start a new one" or "interrupt and replace". Silence, frustration about a delay, or your own
impatience is **not** an override.
